## 343. Intger Break
## Leetcode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/integer-break/
##Intuition:

We want to break n into at least 2 positive integers such that their product is maximum.

Key mathematical insight:

Breaking into larger numbers does NOT maximize product.

Breaking into smaller equal parts increases product.

Among all numbers, 3 gives the maximum multiplication growth.

Example:

2 + 2 + 2 = 6 → product = 8
3 + 3 = 6 → product = 9  ✅ bigger

So we prefer breaking into as many 3s as possible.

 Why 3 is Optimal?

Mathematically:

3 × (n-3) gives better product than 2 × (n-2)

Also, breaking numbers > 4 is always beneficial

But breaking 4 into 2+2 is fine (product stays 4)

So the rule becomes:

 Keep taking 3
 Handle remainder carefully

## Approach

If n == 2 → return 1

If n == 3 → return 2
(Because at least 2 numbers are required)

Divide n by 3:

x = floor(n / 3)
rem = n % 3

Handle remainder:

If rem == 0 → answer = 3^x

If rem == 1 → convert one 3 + 1 into 2 + 2
(because 3×1 = 3 but 2×2 = 4 → better)
→ reduce x by 1 and multiply by 4

If rem == 2 → multiply by 2

##Complexity

Time: O(1) (just math operations)

Space: O(1)
*/
/**
 * @param {number} n
 * @return {number}
 */
var integerBreak = function(n) {
    let pow=0;
    if(n==2)return 1;
    else if(n==3)return 2;
    else if(n==4)return 4;
    else{
        let x=Math.floor(n/3);
        let rem=n%3;
        if(rem==1){
            x--;
            rem+=3;
        }
        pow=Math.pow(3,x);
        if(rem!=0)
        pow*=rem;
    }
    return pow;
};
